    "aegean.vowels"
  ],
  "xp": 2,
  "viz": [
    "sc-grid",
    "sc-signs"
  ],
  "figureArchetype": "GeneralFigure",
  "lesson": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "With the vowels from <a href=\"/ancient-scripts/linear-a-and-b/vowels/\">The Five Vowel Signs</a> in hand, you can learn the consonant rows. Each row is one consonant followed by each of the five vowels. This lesson covers five full rows: d, k, m, n and p."
      },
      {
        "t": "key",
        "html": "Each row is one consonant with the five vowels: da de di do du, ka ke ki ko ku, ma me mi mo mu, na ne ni no nu, pa pe pi po pu. Every cell has its own shape to learn."
      },
      {
        "t": "table",
        "head": [
          "Row",
          "a",
          "e",
          "i",
          "o",
          "u"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "d-",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀅</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">da</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀆</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">de</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀇</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">di</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀈</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">do</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀉</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">du</span>"
          ],
          [
            "k-",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀏</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">ka</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀐</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">ke</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀑</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">ki</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀒</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">ko</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀓</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">ku</span>"
          ],
          [
            "m-",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀔</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">ma</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀕</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">me</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀖</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">mi</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀗</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">mo</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀘</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">mu</span>"
          ],
          [
            "n-",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀙</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">na</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀚</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">ne</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀛</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">ni</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀜</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">no</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀝</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">nu</span>"
          ],
          [
            "p-",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀞</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">pa</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀟</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">pe</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀠</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">pi</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀡</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">po</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀢</span><br><span class=\"sc-tl\">pu</span>"
          ]
        ],
        "cap": "Five consonant rows of Linear B. Every cell is filled."
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "sc-grid",
        "opts": {
          "rows": [
            "d",
            "k",
            "m",
            "n",
            "p"
          ]
        },
        "cap": "Tap any sign for its number and words that use it."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "What the letters mean"
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "The row letters are the transliteration, not exact sounds. The d row is d. The m and n rows are m and n. But the k row also writes g and kh, and the p row also writes b and ph, because Linear B did not keep those sounds apart. <span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.2em;line-height:1\">𐀏𐀒</span> is <i>khalkos</i> (bronze) and <span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.2em;line-height:1\">𐀞𐀏𐀙</span> is <i>phasgana</i> (swords). You will see why in <a href=\"/ancient-scripts/linear-a-and-b/sound-mergers/\">One Sign, Several Sounds</a>."
      },
      {
        "t": "table",
        "head": [
          "Signs",
          "Read",
          "Greek",
          "Meaning"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.4em;line-height:1\">𐀏𐀒</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-tl\">ka-ko</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-gr\" lang=\"grc\">χαλκός</span> <i>khalkos</i>",
            "bronze"
          ],
          [
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.4em;line-height:1\">𐀞𐀳</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-tl\">pa-te</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-gr\" lang=\"grc\">πατήρ</span> <i>pater</i>",
            "father"
          ],
          [
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.4em;line-height:1\">𐀔𐀳</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-tl\">ma-te</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-gr\" lang=\"grc\">μήτηρ</span> <i>meter</i>",
            "mother"
          ],
          [
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.4em;line-height:1\">𐀒𐀜𐀰</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-tl\">ko-no-so</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-gr\" lang=\"grc\">Κνωσός</span> <i>Knosos</i>",
            "Knossos"
          ],
          [
            "<span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.4em;line-height:1\">𐀇𐀞</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-tl\">di-pa</span>",
            "<span class=\"sc-gr\" lang=\"grc\">δέπας</span> <i>depas</i>",
            "cup, goblet"
          ]
        ],
        "cap": "Words spelled with these rows and the vowels."
      },
      {
        "t": "why",
        "html": "Why learn sign by sign instead of by row? Because the shapes do not follow the grid. The grid groups signs by sound, but the signs were inherited from Linear A, where their shapes had their own history. <span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.2em;line-height:1\">𐀏</span> (a circle with a cross) and <span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.2em;line-height:1\">𐀐</span> share nothing in their drawing. So the grid tells you what a sign means once you know it; it cannot tell you how to recognize it."
      },
      {
        "t": "mistake",
        "html": "Expecting signs in one row to look alike. <span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.2em;line-height:1\">𐀏 𐀐 𐀑 𐀒 𐀓</span> all begin with k, yet they look nothing like each other. Check: learn each sign with an anchor word: ka from <span class=\"sc-tl\">ka-ko</span>, ko from <span class=\"sc-tl\">ko-no-so</span>, pa from <span class=\"sc-tl\">pa-te</span>, ma from <span class=\"sc-tl\">ma-te</span>, di from <span class=\"sc-tl\">di-pa</span>."
      },
      {
        "t": "ex",
        "title": "Read a word",
        "q": "Read <span class=\"sc-b\" style=\"font-size:1.5em;line-height:1\">𐀔𐀳</span>.",
        "steps": [
          "The first sign is ma (the m row, a column).",
          "The second is te (the t row, e column)."
        ],
        "a": "<span class=\"sc-tl\">ma-te</span>, <i>mater</i>, mother"
      },
      {
        "t": "ex",
        "title": "Spell from the grid",
        "q": "Write the value in the n row and the o column, then the d row and the a column.",
        "steps": [
          "n + o = no.",
          "d + a = da."
        ],
        "a": "<span class=\"sc-tl\">no</span>, <span class=\"sc-tl\">da</span>"
      },
      {
        "t": "note",
        "html": "You do not have to learn every sign at once. Learn the vowels and two or three rows well, then add rows. The <a href=\"/languages/linear-b/flashcards/\">flashcards</a> have a deck for each row."
      },
      {
        "t": "try"
      }
    ],
